# What a debugger is not shown (design.md §3.1; panel 213's R1, provisional,
# author ratification pending): the word the emitter writes before a C local
# it invented, so that a frame stopped on an author's line lists the author's
# parameters and bindings alone, and the line each unit defines it by.
#
# WHAT CARRIES IT. Every temporary, and every slot of kind `synthetic_slot`
# or `return_slot`, which the prologue declares (`emit/prologue.hero` says
# how the slot's kind decides). And every scratch local the emitter declares
# inside a body, in the block of one instruction: a map lookup's `found`
# (`emit/container.hero`), a text made of bytes' `hero_vb_status` and
# `hero_vb_text` (`emit/bytes_text.hero`), a kept result's `hero_when`
# (`emit/ops.hero`), a handle's `hero_life_<n>_<k>`
# (`emit/handle_before.hero`), and a lent buffer's `hero_lend_b<tag>` and
# `hero_lend_e<tag>` (`emit/lend_buffer.hero`). A frame stopped inside such a
# block, `up` from the call the block makes, listed them beside the author's.
# NOT the generated functions no author's line belongs to, a per-type
# function, a callback's thunk, `hero_extern_refs` and the two `main`s: a
# frame there holds no binding of the author's to keep apart from them.
#
# A HIDDEN DECLARATION CANNOT SHOW A WRONG VALUE: it has no entry in the debug
# information at all, so the debugger has no name to print and no place to
# read; what is lost is the variable, never the truth of one shown. The word
# is the unit's own, defined beside `HERO_TU_LOCAL` (`emit/decls.hero`), so
# neither the runtime's header nor its ABI stamp moves; clang honours the
# attribute in DWARF and in CodeView (the sitting's critic: this Mac, Linux
# arm64's clang 22.1.8, and a Windows target's object).

# The word, and the space after it, written before a declaration.
constant MARK: str
    "HERO_NODEBUG "

# The line each unit's preamble defines the word by.
constant DEFINE: str
    "#define HERO_NODEBUG __attribute__((nodebug))"
